          "text": "Cyclohexanone reacts with methylmagnesium bromide, then phosphoryl trichloride, forming1-methylcyclohexene and methylenecyclohexane in 9: 1 ratio. It also reacts with methylenenetriphenylphosphorane and tetrahydrofuran to form methylenecyclohexane and Ph 3 P O."
